From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zinee-u <suzinee.u@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 00:00:02 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: wifi: ameba: export single-core RX entry

The AmebaD single-core Wi-Fi archive calls eth_rtk_rx() directly. Keeping the
driver implementation static makes CONFIG_SINGLE_CORE_WIFI fail to link even
though the dual-core callback registration path compiles.

Declare and export the entry point expected by the archive, and reject an
invalid interface index before indexing driver state. This remains an internal
driver/vendor-library ABI.

Signed-off-by: zinee-u <suzinee.u@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi.h     | 1 +
 drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi_drv.c | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi.h b/drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi.h
--- a/drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi.h
+++ b/drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi.h
@@ -81,6 +81,7 @@ enum rtk_state_flag {
 };
 
 void wifi_init(void);
+int eth_rtk_rx(uint8_t idx, void *buffer, uint16_t len);
 int wifi_get_scan_records(unsigned int *AP_num, char *scan_buf);
 int wifi_get_mac_address(int idx, struct _rtw_mac_t *mac, uint8_t efuse);
 int rltk_wlan_send(int idx, void *pkt_addr, uint32_t len);
diff --git a/drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi_drv.c b/drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi_drv.c
--- a/drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/wifi/ameba/ameba_wifi_drv.c
@@ -107,10 +107,15 @@ static int ameba_wifi_send(const struct device *dev, struct net_pkt *pkt)
 }
 
 /* should called in driver after rx */
-static int eth_rtk_rx(uint8_t idx, void *buffer, uint16_t len)
+int eth_rtk_rx(uint8_t idx, void *buffer, uint16_t len)
 {
 	struct net_pkt *pkt;
 
+	if (idx >= ARRAY_SIZE(ameba_wifi_iface)) {
+		LOG_ERR("invalid network interface index: %u", idx);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	if (ameba_wifi_iface[idx] == NULL) {
 		LOG_ERR("network interface unavailable");
 		return -EIO;
-- 
